.TH DEVX 1
.SH NAME
devx \- macOS project, worktree, and local configuration overlay navigator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devx
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B devx
opens Git projects and worktrees, creates worktrees, and applies local
configuration overlays without storing local settings in project repositories.
Configuration is stored in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/devx ,
or
.IR ~/.config/devx
when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is not set.
.SH INSTALLATION
Install the binary from a checkout:
.PP
.EX
cargo install --path .
.EE
.PP
Interactive commands require fzf:
.PP
.EX
brew install fzf
.EE
.PP
All fzf prompts match case-insensitively. Press Esc to cancel a picker, or
Ctrl+C at any prompt to stop devx and its active child process. devx does not
continue to later writes after cancellation.
.SH QUICK START
For first-time setup, run
.B devx setup
to discover applications in /Applications, ~/Applications, and Homebrew Cask,
choose application roles, add scan roots, refresh the project cache, and
optionally install the Raycast command. All selections are stored in config.toml.
.PP
Register directories containing repositories, then refresh the cached list when
repositories or externally-created worktrees change. Clones and worktrees made
by devx refresh the cache automatically.
.PP
.EX
devx project add-root ~/dev
devx project refresh
.EE
.TP
.B devx launcher edit
Interactively update the IDE/editor, terminal, configuration editor, and
Raycast terminal applications without changing projects or overlays.
.TP
.B devx launcher list
Print the configured launcher commands.
.TP
.B devx reset
After confirmation, remove all devx configuration and overlays. Repositories
and Git worktrees are never changed.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS AND COMPLETIONS
.B devx doctor
checks Git, fzf, configured applications, local configuration, and the Raycast
script command. Missing dependencies include a resolution command.
.PP
.B devx completions zsh
and
.B devx completions fish
write shell completion scripts to standard output. For zsh, save the result to
~/.zfunc/_devx and add ~/.zfunc to fpath before running compinit. For fish,
save it to ~/.config/fish/completions/devx.fish.
.SH PROJECTS
.TP
.B devx project add PATH [--name NAME]
Register a checkout outside scan roots or give one an explicit alias.
.TP
.B devx project add-root PATH [--name NAME]
Register a directory to scan recursively for Git repositories when refreshed.
.TP
.B devx project refresh
Refresh the cached repository and worktree list from all registered scan roots.
.TP
.B devx project list
List registered and discovered repositories and worktrees.
.TP
.B devx project remove NAME
Remove an explicitly registered project. It does not delete files.
.TP
.B devx project clone ROOT URL
Clone a repository beneath a named scan root without opening applications.
.TP
.B devx open NAME [--no-editor] [--no-terminal]
Open a checkout in the configured editor and terminal.
.TP
.B devx pick
Use fzf to select and open checkouts, create worktrees, set up overlays, or
apply overlays. Opening ranks repository groups by previous usage before fzf
filters them. Pickers use compact tables with headers. Narrow terminals show
name, branch, state, and checkout type; terminals at least 100 columns wide
also show the home-relative path.
.SH WORKTREES
.B devx worktree create PROJECT BRANCH [--name NAME]
fetches origin, resolves its default branch, creates a new branch, and puts the
worktree under the scan-root sibling layout:
.PP
.EX
~/dev/.worktrees/my-service/feature-login
.EE
.PP
Existing worktrees are discovered with Git and are not moved. New worktrees
share their primary project's configuration overlays and open in the configured
editor and terminal after creation.
.SH CONFIGURATION OVERLAYS
Set up a project once. With no project argument, fzf selects a checkout.
.PP
.EX
devx project setup my-service
.EE
.PP
Select one or more existing .yml, .yaml, .properties, or .env files. For each,
devx creates empty overlays with the same project-relative path:
.PP
.EX
~/.config/devx/configs/global/src/main/resources/bootstrap.yml
~/.config/devx/configs/my-service/src/main/resources/bootstrap.yml
.EE
.PP
The project directory is opened with the lightweight configuration editor,
which defaults to Zed. Configure it in config.toml as a token array:
.PP
.EX
[launchers]
config_editor = ["open", "-a", "Zed", "{path}"]
.EE
.TP
.B devx config global-add
Prompt for a supported project-relative filename and create an empty global
overlay. A global overlay affects only projects mapped to that relative path.
.TP
.B devx config list PROJECT
List configuration files mapped for a project and its worktrees.
.TP
.B devx config apply PROJECT
Merge and preview all mapped files as one batch, then request one confirmation
before writing any files.
.PP
Precedence is base project file, then global overlay, then project overlay.
YAML overlays use nested mappings only. Mappings merge recursively, scalars
replace scalars, and lists replace lists. Dotted YAML overlay keys, duplicate
keys, and YAML type conflicts fail before any write. YAML formatting and
comments are normalized after a semantic merge.
.PP
.properties and .env overlays merge by key. Later layers replace earlier
values, new keys are appended, and unchanged base lines and comments remain.
Duplicate keys in any input fail before writes.
.properties support is limited to one logical key=value or key:value entry per
line; escaped separators, escaped keys, and line continuations are unsupported.
.SH LAUNCHERS
The default configuration opens IntelliJ IDEA and Ghostty. All launchers
are token arrays; {path} is replaced safely with the project directory.
.PP
.EX
[launchers]
editor = ["open", "-a", "IntelliJ IDEA", "{path}"]
terminal = ["open", "-a", "Ghostty", "{path}"]
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/devx/config.toml
Project registry, scan roots, usage history, launcher configuration, and
managed overlay mappings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/devx/configs/
Global and project-specific overlay files.
.SH SEE ALSO
Run
.B devx --help
or
.B devx COMMAND --help
for clap-generated command and option reference.
.SH RAYCAST
Run devx raycast install to install a bundled Raycast Script Command under
~/Library/Application Support/Raycast/Script Commands/devx. Add that directory
in Raycast Settings, Extensions, Script Commands, Add Directory, then assign
Devx Pick a hotkey. It starts devx pick in Ghostty.
The launcher is configurable with [launchers].raycast_terminal.
